  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to foster implementation of Sabahs Orangutan Action Plan. This will be done by: 1. developing information on trends in distribution, population densities and conservation status of the orangutan and other wildlife in several key areas in Sabah; 2. documenting the processes of ecological adaptation of the orangutan to degraded and fragmented habitat; 3. obtaining a better understanding of the patterns of use of oil palm plantation landscapes by orangutans; 4. formulating and achieving agreement with stakeholders on policies based on scientific knowledge for long-term conservation in Sabah; 5. achieving support and recognition for Sabahs efforts towards orangutan conservation; 5. reducing levels of degradation and fragmentation of orangutan habitats through improved land use management; 6. empowering indigenous communities in the management of local natural resources; 7. having model community initiatives lead to socio-economic and conservation gains; 8. enhancing local capabilities among Malaysian conservation professionals; and 9. raising the level of environmental awareness among stakeholders, general public and school children.</narrative>
  </description>
